`FoundationClassifier` takes any class labels, as a scikit-learn classifier does: it trains on the index of each label in `classes_` and predicts the labels. It passed the labels to the network as they were, so text labels raised a `TypeError` and integer labels other than 0 to n_classes - 1, such as 1 and 2, raised `IndexError: Target 2 is out of bounds`, as did a training fold missing one of the classes in between. `Experiment` encodes its targets first and was not affected.
